\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{A Lean program (\code{lake exe forest-export}) walks the environment for every module under \code{Kernel/}, \code{Root/}, \code{Interface/}, \code{Theory/} and emits one \code{.tree} per non-private declaration into \code{build/forest/} (gitignored, rebuilt in CI). Each node has:}
  \ul{
    \li{title: fully qualified name; taxon from the declaration kind (\code{Definition}, \code{Theorem}, \code{Lemma}, \code{Structure}, \code{Class}, \code{Instance}, \code{Opaque});}
    \li{the statement (pretty-printed signature in a code block) and the docstring;}
    \li{status: \code{proved} / \code{sorry} (from \code{collectAxioms}), plus \code{sealed} if in \code{Interface/}, \code{kernel} if in \code{Kernel/};}
    \li{dependencies: nodes for each constant used in the type and, for theorems, in the proof (from \code{Expr.getUsedConstants}), split into "in statement" and "in proof";}
    \li{dependents (reverse index, computed after the walk);}
    \li{source link with line range (from \code{declaration_ranges});}
    \li{the decisions it cites (from a \code{@[decision D-RT-03]}-style attribute or a docstring tag).}
  }
  \p{Addresses are deterministic from the name (hash-suffixed) so links survive renames of the file layout but not of the declaration.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Agents will navigate by dependency and status, not by file. Humans will read prose that transcludes these.}
}
\subtree{
